  "readmeFile": "PACKAGE.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Streaming robustness and performance. A streamed transform now observes the CancellationToken across its streaming and whole-input-buffer loops, so a long-running or unbounded transform cancels promptly instead of running to completion. xsl:try no longer snapshots the whole accumulated output buffer on every attempt — it checkpoints by length and truncates on rollback (O(1)), so error-catching inside a streamed loop over a large input is linear rather than quadratic (a per-item xsl:try over 100K items is dramatically faster). Picks up PhoenixmlDb.Core 1.2.1, whose XML parser computes a large element's string value in linear time. Requires PhoenixmlDb.Core 1.2.1 and PhoenixmlDb.XQuery 1.5.3. No API changes. See RELEASES.md for full notes.",
